# PainLocator Engineering Constitution

PainLocator is not a generic demo application. It is a professional clinical software platform built on the **Clinical Anatomy Engine (CAE)**.

Every architectural, UI, and engineering decision must support this long-term vision.

## CAE Ecosystem Principle (critical)

**PainLocator is a flagship application built on CAE.** The engine must remain **reusable** so future healthcare applications can use the same rendering, coordinate mapping, annotation, reporting, and AI infrastructure **without modification**.

- `src/engine/` = reusable CAE (no PainLocator workflow logic)
- `src/features/`, `src/app/` = PainLocator application
- Never duplicate engine capabilities in app code

## Product philosophy

Prioritize: clinical clarity, patient ease, physician efficiency, accessibility, maintainability, extensibility, professional presentation. Quality over quantity. Every feature must solve a real clinical workflow.

## UX

Anatomy is always the primary focus. Calm, uncluttered, progressive disclosure. Professional medical software — not a control dashboard.

## Workflows

Every feature belongs to one: **Capture** (log pain), **Review** (history/timeline), **Clinical Analysis** (AI, reporting, clinical tools). If unclear, reconsider placement.

## CAE rules

Normalized coordinates (0–1). Decouple rendering from annotation. No duplicated coordinate logic. Region detection independent of assets.

## UI

Majority screen space for anatomy. Theme tokens only — never hardcode colors. WCAG contrast. Toolbar readable in light and dark.

## Annotations

Entries contain regions/points/polygons. Editable: move, resize, delete, rename, recolor. Hierarchy: Markers → Entries → Sessions → Patients.

## Reporting

Clinical-grade reports. PDF (print), JSON, PNG. Never expose debug info in reports.

## JSON

Schema version required. Backward compatibility via versioning. Document in `docs/JSON_SCHEMA.md`.

## AI

Assistive only — never diagnostic. Label: "Assistive Clinical Observation — Not a Medical Diagnosis."

## Code

Maintainability over speed. Small modules. Conventional Commits. `npm run build` must pass before milestone commits.

## Final principle

Never sacrifice long-term maintainability for short-term speed. Build for an ecosystem of clinical applications on CAE.

**Full constitution:** `ENGINEERING_PRINCIPLES.md` (repository root)
